// Bound claims manifest — rung R1 of the self-falsifying compilation line.
// Spec: docs/research/self_falsifying_compilation_line_r1_2026-07-26.md
//
// This is the first file in the repository outside tests/ and CI fixtures to
// carry native `claim` blocks bound to REAL CI gates. Compiling it with
// --verify-claims executes every gate below before codegen; if any gate goes
// red the compiler refuses to emit an ELF.
//
//   artifacts/self-hosted/madaros-self-falsifying run \
//       examples/epistemic/rupture_claims_verified.sio -o /tmp/x.elf --verify-claims
//
// WHY A MANIFEST AND NOT THE LIBRARIES THEMSELVES. The mechanism executes only
// the claims of the *main source file* — an imported module's claims are never
// run (measured, not assumed: scripts/ci/fixtures/self_falsifying_modclosure_*.sio
// compiles cleanly while importing a module whose claim's gate always fails).
// Claims therefore cannot yet live where the science lives. Hoisting them into
// a manifest compiled by CI is the workaround the limitation forces, and this
// file is also the evidence of its cost.
//
// HONESTY. Each hypothesis below states only that the named contract's clauses
// hold — which is exactly what its gate checks. None of them restates the
// underlying mathematical result; a claim bound to a gate may assert no more
// than the gate establishes. Gates exceeding the executor's 30 s wall-clock
// timeout are excluded by construction and listed in the spec.

claim founder_intent_contract_holds {
    hypothesis = "the founder-intent contract clauses hold in the working tree",
    falsifier  = "scripts/ci/founder_intent_contract_gate.sh exits non-zero",
    evidence   = Evidence::GateGreen,
    harness    = "scripts/ci/founder_intent_contract_gate.sh",
    gate       = "scripts/ci/founder_intent_contract_gate.sh",
    verdict    = Verdict::Alive,
}

claim generated_ontology_manifest_consistent {
    hypothesis = "the generated ontology manifest is consistent with its sources",
    falsifier  = "scripts/ci/generated_ontology_manifest_gate.sh exits non-zero",
    evidence   = Evidence::GateGreen,
    harness    = "scripts/ci/generated_ontology_manifest_gate.sh",
    gate       = "scripts/ci/generated_ontology_manifest_gate.sh",
    verdict    = Verdict::Alive,
}

